                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ace958a0-ec52-3a57-b54e-9bf01a347460",
                        "entry_id": "7c666123-b8bb-3606-b105-346c30c77495",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. уныние, хандра; тоскливое настроение"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c9132c48-d532-4eeb-b1f6-a618ccb5d826",
                                "sense_id": "ace958a0-ec52-3a57-b54e-9bf01a347460",
                                "text": "Я надеюсь, что воздух моей гостиной разгонит ваш сплин… не правда ли?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a9382dc4-55ad-4a1e-bb23-54fd1bb8296c",
                                "sense_id": "ace958a0-ec52-3a57-b54e-9bf01a347460",
                                "text": "Это чувство мучило меня с тех пор, как я начал себя помнить, и я ему приписываю те минуты сплина, которые докторам угодно приписывать желчи."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dcfef8d8-b803-49dc-b0af-c4d5c761e496",
                                "sense_id": "ace958a0-ec52-3a57-b54e-9bf01a347460",
                                "text": "― Я не верю его любви; он, как англичанин, чудак, занимался Индианой от нечего делать, чтоб разогнать, может быть, свой сплин."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5fb859f7-9e4d-4e75-8b88-2735b8b50c45",
                        "source_entry_id": "7c666123-b8bb-3606-b105-346c30c77495",
                        "source_sense_id": "ace958a0-ec52-3a57-b54e-9bf01a347460",
                        "target_lang_word": "spleen",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "spleen",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f16e9319-1be7-3735-86f9-f9564c04d2fe",
                                        "entry_id": "99aca4b7-4b3a-3b4a-9ef5-df4dfa141489",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In vertebrates, including humans, a ductless vascular gland, located in the left upper abdomen near the stomach, which destroys old red blood cells, removes debris from the bloodstream, acts as a reservoir of blood, and produces lymphocytes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "40d3145d-ba26-37dd-9f4d-e003d5d693c2",
                                        "entry_id": "99aca4b7-4b3a-3b4a-9ef5-df4dfa141489",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bad mood; spitefulness. Compare gall."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "772d571c-34e7-456c-9adf-752dfb8de5b3",
                                                "sense_id": "40d3145d-ba26-37dd-9f4d-e003d5d693c2",
                                                "text": "In noble minds some dregs remain, / Not yet purged off, of spleen and sour disdain."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1dcc487-8857-45c2-b15c-126c1eb01f00",
                                                "sense_id": "40d3145d-ba26-37dd-9f4d-e003d5d693c2",
                                                "text": "Too many, however, who might take an honourable stand, fear the petty spleen of the plantocracy; preferring the most disgusting adulation, to the blessing of him ready to perish."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "645248c9-546f-4429-bb28-7af467bf957b",
                                                "sense_id": "40d3145d-ba26-37dd-9f4d-e003d5d693c2",
                                                "text": "The name I like best, however, I heard uttered by the Eldest Son of the House of Chou, who in a moment of spleen referred to his colleague of the House of Liang as hsiao chu-tan, the Little Pig’s Egg."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "663d733d-e401-4806-b6e7-c8d8549f9085",
                                                "sense_id": "40d3145d-ba26-37dd-9f4d-e003d5d693c2",
                                                "text": "Sullen now, with stultified spleen, Mrs Dibble grappled her crutches and levered herself upright after an ungainly struggle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "497d7bbc-7258-38d0-8f34-4d79c9c2606f",
                                        "entry_id": "99aca4b7-4b3a-3b4a-9ef5-df4dfa141489",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sudden motion or action; a fit; a freak; a whim."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "rare",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8b1e997-1477-4c84-92a4-743f45c5dbb3",
                                                "sense_id": "497d7bbc-7258-38d0-8f34-4d79c9c2606f",
                                                "text": "A thousand spleens bear her a thousand ways.\nBrief as the lightning in the collied night; That, in a spleen, unfolds both heaven and Earth"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a0bde34c-cc8d-3688-9e75-4178f8664c68",
                                        "entry_id": "99aca4b7-4b3a-3b4a-9ef5-df4dfa141489",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Melancholy; hypochondriacal affections."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eab70f37-915d-4775-84b6-a276f025971a",
                                                "sense_id": "a0bde34c-cc8d-3688-9e75-4178f8664c68",
                                                "text": "Bodies changed to various forms by spleen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2bc63ba3-2f79-4683-bece-be533c91e82c",
                                                "sense_id": "a0bde34c-cc8d-3688-9e75-4178f8664c68",
                                                "text": "There is a luxury in self-dispraise: / And inward self-disparagement affords / To meditative spleen a grateful feast."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8c34ae73-e830-34c6-99a4-d6b7e4c613fd",
                                        "entry_id": "99aca4b7-4b3a-3b4a-9ef5-df4dfa141489",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fit of immoderate laughter or merriment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5173bd6e-0086-49c7-870e-4eff66fbbb25",
                                                "sense_id": "8c34ae73-e830-34c6-99a4-d6b7e4c613fd",
                                                "text": "By virtue, thou enforcest laughter ; thy silly thought, my spleen"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "spleen",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "22e5b799-f9c4-3e0b-b8f4-67f1b437b954",
                                        "entry_id": "a2087cf0-7111-307d-b425-2a8c3d526e3c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To dislike."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0005dcfd-5156-47d2-8eec-96c5040af156",
                                                "sense_id": "22e5b799-f9c4-3e0b-b8f4-67f1b437b954",
                                                "text": "T. Wentworth ſpleen'd the Bishop"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ca51acdc-ebce-31e7-a167-f1c5cd1e8b34",
                                        "entry_id": "a2087cf0-7111-307d-b425-2a8c3d526e3c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To annoy or irritate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7cfa1410-76c1-48d0-86ea-884716a1a0ac",
                                                "sense_id": "ca51acdc-ebce-31e7-a167-f1c5cd1e8b34",
                                                "text": "There had been a good deal of provocation, we have no doubt, before the republican simplicity, at which Mrs Trollope seems to have been so justly offended, was spleened into speaking of the old woman."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f46aae04-2cb0-4e67-8d17-75c88ebbc143",
                                                "sense_id": "ca51acdc-ebce-31e7-a167-f1c5cd1e8b34",
                                                "text": "If you want to know why I am always spleening her, it is because I am always elsewhere with friends, and disseminating so much currency, and performing so many things that can spleen a mother."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7f85076a-1da0-3028-9d50-fa38caa826ca",
                                        "entry_id": "a2087cf0-7111-307d-b425-2a8c3d526e3c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To complain; to rail; to vent one's spleen."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c231e5f7-6ff8-48a1-a84c-7398d4bb9f70",
                                                "sense_id": "7f85076a-1da0-3028-9d50-fa38caa826ca",
                                                "text": "It was satisfactory to a majority of the bolters, but most of the democrats spleened against him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54d2b06e-3be0-47da-9a5a-c9d92c189657",
                                                "sense_id": "7f85076a-1da0-3028-9d50-fa38caa826ca",
                                                "text": "He never counseled litigation for the sake of litigation, and no client ever complained of his loyalty, He hated sham and pretense, and openly spleened at the empty mouthing oracle of the street corner, the society, or the church."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "117b18ae-dffb-499d-b562-42d504ec1344",
                                                "sense_id": "7f85076a-1da0-3028-9d50-fa38caa826ca",
                                                "text": "O Captain, my Captain, I shan't migrain that fight —A teritable Dunga Minh art thou, A phantom of loneflight; And though I've swaggered you and spleened you, By the living bilge that gleaned you — You're a better man than I am, Dunga Minh!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d11074b1-ffcd-4be8-aac0-e8fdcf6b76f6",
                                                "sense_id": "7f85076a-1da0-3028-9d50-fa38caa826ca",
                                                "text": "When he phoned the old man in Idaho, Herman Zaunbrecher spleened “no dothead fucking quack's gonna treat my boy like a lab rat” and ordered the surgeon to put Randall on the next flight to Boise."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "99083b2d-1894-3dff-b758-acd7f1ef10d0",
                                        "entry_id": "a2087cf0-7111-307d-b425-2a8c3d526e3c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To remove the spleen, or, by extension, to gore."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "feeaafc2-7252-4761-aeaf-8b2a98c510cd",
                                                "sense_id": "99083b2d-1894-3dff-b758-acd7f1ef10d0",
                                                "text": "Nor did they only take Townes, kill such as made resistance, and rob houses, with the Licentiousnesse and Avarice of Souldiers, but with barbarous Inhumanity spared no age nor modesty; tyrannizing over the Rest and Monuments of the dead, which they spleened as much as the Living;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ecae7d2-b30d-4fff-b70f-9e9fe77d33f4",
                                                "sense_id": "99083b2d-1894-3dff-b758-acd7f1ef10d0",
                                                "text": "I grant a good deal to Grecian pride of prose, and Roman fund of poesy, when spleened and gored to shame, defeat, and loss of prestige, on the battle-field by mere \"barbaric\" ( ? ) troops of Cimbric Hyperborean Celts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "efe08e58-a4e9-4386-b106-1baf5d8282e0",
                                                "sense_id": "99083b2d-1894-3dff-b758-acd7f1ef10d0",
                                                "text": "\"That is true,\" quoth Albertu, “but pray consider on the other side that animals spleened grow extremely salacious, an experiment well known in dogs.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "306ba92e-c9c2-3b39-b303-9899b46ee624",
                                        "entry_id": "a2087cf0-7111-307d-b425-2a8c3d526e3c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To excise or remove."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53aef373-3ed8-41dd-82dc-bd708f38e9c8",
                                                "sense_id": "306ba92e-c9c2-3b39-b303-9899b46ee624",
                                                "text": "That will be how we lose what we have gained, The incremental rapture at the core, Spleened of the belly's thick placental wrath, And the seed's roar."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "683c109c-a304-41ec-b6c2-882af160324d",
                                                "sense_id": "306ba92e-c9c2-3b39-b303-9899b46ee624",
                                                "text": "Picking up where I left off...broken down, knowing they'd pick through my bones like vultures for what marrow they hadn't already spleened from me."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21e5e61f-0c68-40d9-bfc3-3a78f8a34ade",
                                                "sense_id": "306ba92e-c9c2-3b39-b303-9899b46ee624",
                                                "text": "There is even a subtle reference to sexuality in the poem, but it is formulated in such a manner that it is spleened of all vulgarity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
